Jack Bolsen <jbolsen@verizon.net> wrote:

>A bookstore was on the minetown level. I promptly killed the proprietor 
>and took his possessions. Naturally, I felt compelled to read the books. 
>Compelled, until after trying to read one I got the message "you notice 
>you have no gold!" Ouch - I had around 13,000gp! 

Reading unblessed spellbooks may be a risk, but a calculable risk. A
book's base price is level*100, and your chance of succesfully reading an
uncursed spellbook depends only on your experience level and the spell's
level (assuming fixed INT).

>Yes, it was an annoying death, but I got a kick out of it when the list 
>of monsters killed listed *6* shopkeepers!

Shopkeepers are very valuable for price-identifying. With the money that
you lost, you could have bought several points of AC, which might have
saved you later on. 
